  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ayad River and lakes restoration.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271080" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Model project for River Restoration</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Sustainable solutions identified and incorporated into tender process for Ayad River"></target>
     <actual value="Achieved with integrated solutions to protect biodiversity and enhance local architecture, heritage and history."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Model project for River Restoration"></target>
     <actual value="Expert meeting, report on model project, report on green-blue Ayad Riverscape, note and workshops completed"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="New project corporation has been initiated on new water body: the 
overflow channel (Gumaniya Nalla) from city lakes to Ayad River"></target>
     <actual value="Partly achieved
- Concept for river rejuvenation of a 1,5 km model stretch is being 
developed 
- Online workshop meeting with UMC. Data collection and drone data to set up the model for further 
modelling and design approach for conceptualization 
Completed 
- The concept of integrating the Ayad river into the city and vice versa 
adding value to the river surroundings have been presented to and 
adopted by the UMC in tenders."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sewage water treatment solutions.</narrative>
   </title>
   <reference code="271081" vocabulary="99"></reference>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Business case for sludge treatment plant at Eklingpura prepared</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Baseline for sludge composition
and evaluation on technical SWT solutions
are possible in terms of integrated
energy production"></target>
     <actual value="Information gathering via the UMC program
validating data regarding possible energy production
from sludge treatment ongoing."></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Sludge monitoring program established for  analysis of both excess- and faecal sludge."></target>
     <actual value="Monitoring and analytical activities to be continued in a new phase"></actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target value="Baseline for sludge composition
and evaluation on technical SWT solutions
are possible in terms of integrated
energy production"></target>
     <actual value="Partly achieved.
A factfinding has been completed, as basis for a preliminary input to a business
case on energy production at Eklingpura STP as for an input to a business case
for collection and reuse of septic sludge.
It is decided to continue with an actual business case for sludge to energy
production, while the frame for a possible business case for sludge collection from
septic tanks is still discussed.
Regarding the business case for sludge to energy production, there has been
prepared a Baseline Study report by CRISIL in corporation with IUC, UMC and
Aarhus. The report forms the basis of a common understanding on the situation
in Udaipur regarding sewage treatment, sludge production and sludge handling. 
As a next step in preparing a business case a sludge monitoring program has been
set up in corporation with Hindustan Zink. The monitoring program includes
analysis of both excess- and faecal sludge."></actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
